  "steps": [
    "Cook the rice according to the package. Let it cool 10 minutes, then mix in the rice vinegar, sweetener and salt to taste.",
    "Preheat the air fryer to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Toss the chicken with the pepper, soy sauce and egg, then add the cornstarch and toss until every piece is coated.",
    "Spray the chicken and air fry in a single layer (in batches if needed) 10-12 minutes, shaking halfway, until crisp and the thickest piece reads 165°F.",
    "Meanwhile, simmer the glaze ingredients in a large pan over medium heat, stirring, until thick and sticky, 3-5 minutes.",
    "Toss the chicken in the glaze. Serve over the rice with green onions and sesame seeds."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "No air fryer: bake at 425°F (220°C) for 15-18 minutes, flipping halfway.",
    "Serves 4, about 495 cal and 50g protein each.",
    "Keeps 5 days in the fridge. Reheat with 1 tsp water, partially covered, in the microwave for 3 minutes.",
    "The recipe originates with @panaceapalm; the air fryer and oven settings come from his sibling sweet chilli version, which uses the same chicken and coating."
  ],
